From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: qr_screen_bin: snapshot the child once

QrScreenBin::snapshot() called parent_snapshot() twice, so the viewfinder
was rendered twice every frame. Besides the doubled GPU work, the second
copy put a second render node referring to the viewfinder's
GtkGraphicsOffload subsurface into the tree ("Multiple nodes referring to
subsurface" with GDK_DEBUG=offload), which disables offloading the camera
frames to the compositor altogether.
---
--- a/src/widgets/qr_screen_bin.rs
+++ b/src/widgets/qr_screen_bin.rs
@@ -119,8 +119,6 @@
             // compute it's actual size.
             let (inner_w, inner_h) = self.calculate_aspect_ratio(aspect as f32);
 
-            self.parent_snapshot(snapshot);
-
             let Some(animation) = self.dim_ani.get() else {
                 return;
             };
